coly0101	Lleslle: Clint, I wanna bounce off like what you're saying before about the passion that everybody had, because it is. I remember us all just-- It was no big deal to stay the night sometimes, especially towards the end 'cause we were all just trying to fix whatever bugs there were, and just make it better and polished. And I remember some of the conversations that you and I would have about just organization and making sure that, you know, the creative process was supported and all of that. And it just was nice that we all cared about our areas so much, you know?
coly0102	Clint: Absolutely, Lleslle. I think that's really what I was trying to say earlier, is that the goals that everyone set were so high and then they became internalized as the bare minimum. So even though they were beyond necessarily the call of duty, if you will, they were still viewed as must-achieves.
coly0103	Lleslle: Oh yeah, and I think that's like a given on a Tim game thought, right, because his creative, like, bar is so extremely high. And you see him working so much that you just can't-- You can't help it. And especially when you see the game and the story that you're working on, and you want to make sure it's the best. And you can-- Every little nuance, I mean just the music, and like you said, the attention to detail. Just those birds flapping... You know, it's just amazing.
