intma01	Sorry for the wait, Mr. Flores.
intma02	I am ready to take you now.
intcl03	Take me? Take me where?
intma04	Now, now...
intma05	There's no need to be nervous.
intcl06	N-nervous? N-no... I-i-it's just your appearance... It's, well, a little intimidating...
intma07	Intimidating? Me? But I'm your friend! My name's Manny Calavera. I'm your new travel agent!
intcl08	I don't want a new travel agent. I want to go home.
intma09	Ha Ha! You can't go home, Celso. You're dead. But you're not alone...
intma10	Everybody here is just as dead as you.
intma11	That's why we call it the "Land of the Dead."
intma12	Are you ready for your big journey?
intcl13	No!
intcl14	What journey?
intma15	The Four-Year Journey of the Soul. It is quite a big trip. And I can't lie to you, Celso.
intma16	It could be very, very dangerous.
intma17	Unless...you were to take that money you were buried with and buy a better travel package from us!
intma18	I mean, wouldn't you rather cross the Land of the Dead in your own sports car? Maybe try a luxury ocean cruise? Or, if you led a very good life, you may even be eligible for a ticket on the Number Nine itself!
intcl19	The Number Nine?
intma20	That's our top-of-the-line express train. It shoots straight to the Ninth Underworld, the Land of Eternal Rest, in four minutes instead of four years. But very few people qualify. Let's take a look at your records.
intma21	Hmmm?
intma22	Hmmm... Well, the bad news is the train appears to be just out of your reach. But I still got a coupla tricks up my sleeve here...
intma23	Mmm-hmmm... Yah-ha. Yes... That's the ticket...
intma24	...the "EXCELSIOR LINE"!
intma25	Yes, she's a beauty. That compass in the handle will sure come in handy, too...
intma26	Oh, you're going to have a great trip. Wish I was going!
intcl27	Why don't you? You could give me a lift.
intma28	Oh, I can't leave here until I've worked off a little debt to the powers that be...
intcl29	Community service, eh?
intcl30	Well, I guess there are some folks worse off than me.
intma31	Oh, I'll be leaving here soon enough!
intma32	No thanks to dead-end, no-commission, low-life cases like yours, menso.
intev33	Hey, Manny. The boss told me to tell you not to leave early tonight. He wants to talk to you about something when he gets back from his trip.
intma34	Tell Don not to worry...
intma35	...I'm not going anywhere.
intma36	Especially not with clients like that!
intma37	Where do they get these guys? They don't qualify for anything good, so I can't sell anything good, can't work off my time, and I'm stuck. Stuck selling walking sticks to a bunch of burros for eternity.
intma38	I need better clients. I need a real saint. I need a lead on a rich, dead saint.
lolma01	Eva, you gotta give this thing one more go for me.
lolev02	All right, but he sounds pretty mad...
lolev03	Mr. Copal? Mr. Calavera has somethin' out here that he says he needs your signature on--
lolco04	Ah, cripes, Eva! Just sign it yourself, will ya? I'm busy!
lolev05	You'll have to excuse him, Manny. It's probably a really hard crossword puzzle he's got in there today.
lolma06	Eva, I'm impressed.
lolma07	I had no idea you had this kind of power.
lolev08	Well, we all have our secrets.
lolgl09	Gdak. Gahh. Ahh. Nuhh.
lolgl10	Hey, I look good in this, don't I? Heh heh.
lolma11	Yeah, well, they say black is slimming...
lolgl12	I'm drivin'! Yeah! I'm drivin'! RrrrrrrrmmmmmmAahaha!
lolgl13	Brrrrrrr!
lolma14a	Por favor.
brpma01	...but we offer several travel package upgrades if you'd care to--
brpbo02	Cut the yap. I want something cheap where I can get some rest, and that's it.
brpma03	Ay ay ay.
brpgl04	You know, Manny, I could make this car a little faster. If you wanted...
brpma05	Yeah, yeah. Whatever.
brpgl06	Oh yeah, slam the front into the weeds, tub the rear end, dual blowers poppin' outta the hood!
brpgl07	Wah-wah-wah-wah-WAAAAAH! Wah-wah-wah-wah-WAAAAAAAAHAAAAHHH!
brpma08	You'll get plenty of rest this way, Mr. Martinez, and you'll be safely padded by the foam created when these two chemicals mix, like this.
brpbo09	Uh, on second thought, I wanna upgrade my package!
brpma10	Sorry, Bruno, but you didn't qualify for anything better.
brpma11	But here, have this complimentary mug!
brpbo12	No! Wait! Can't you find me something where I can move my legs?
brpma13	You know I'd like to, Bruno...
brpma14	...but my boss is a real hard-ass.
brpco15	I gotta be a hard-ass when I got lazy sickle-wavers like THIS jolly boy working for me! Manny, you couldn't find a sale at a yacht club!
brpma16	I got a sale right here!
brpco17	I'm talkin' PREMIUM sales, Calavera! Like the kind Domino makes!
brpma18	How am I supposed to make premium sales with the scumbag clients you're sending me?
brpbo19	Hey!
brpbo21	Who you callin' a scumbag? Why, I oughta--
rm1ma01	Glottis! Are you loco? What got into you? That was a company car!
rm1gl02	Oh yeah! And it's even better company now! Hop in! Yeeeeaha! Woo!
rm1ma03	Buenos d╝as.
rm1me04	You're not the nurse.
rm1ma05	No.
rm1me06	You're not here to give me my medication?
rm1ma07	No, but I am here to ease your pain.
rm1me08	Guess they couldn't save me, eh?
rm1ma09	No, but there's still a chance you could save me.
rm3co01	Hey!  Funny Bones!  In my office!  Now!
rm3co02	You VANDALIZED company property in order to obtain SECRET INFORMATION so you could take your ILLEGALLY MODIFIED company car and your UNREGISTERED DRIVER and run Domino here off the road--
rm3co03	--all in order to steal a client from her legitimate agent!
rm3ma04	There's nothing legitimate about this place. You give all the good clients to Domino.
rm3do11	Manny, now I'm embarrassed for you.
rm3co05	You've embarrassed the whole office. I'm going to call the woman in here so you can apologize to her yourself.
rm3co06	Eva, send in Ms. Colomar, please.
rm3ev07	She left about fifteen minutes ago, sir. She said she had a long walk ahead of her and she wanted to get started.
rm3co08	Walking? She had a ticket on the Number Nine! Why does she think she has to walk?
rm3ma09	That's the best package I could find for her...
rm3co11	That woman was a saint and a shoe-in for a Double-N ticket that she's not going to get because YOU...
rm3co12	...just couldn't find it! And now, because of your little stunt, she's out there...
rm3co13	...on her own...
rm3co15	Get in there and stay put until the boys downtown tell us what they want done with ya.  Someone's gonna take the fall for this, Calavera, and it ain't gonna be me!
lq_ma01	I'm going to blow the lid off this place!
lq_sv02	Young man, you are an enemy of the Department of Death!
lsasv01	Salvador Limones and guest.
lsama02	Where are you taking me?
lsasv03	To the headquarters of the LSA.
lsama04	LSA?
lsasv05	The Lost Souls' Alliance. We're a small group, Manuel, but we're always looking for new soldiers.
lsama06	To do what, exactly?
lsasv07	We need help in our intelligence unit. You know Eva, of course.
lsasv08	I was once a reaper like yourself, Manuel. But I uncovered a web of corruption in our beloved Department of Death.
lsama10	What's your evidence?
lsasv11	That's where you come in, Manuel. Or should I call you "Agent Calavera"?
lsama12	"Manny" suits me fine. I'm not looking to join any military organization, Sal. I just want my job back so I can work off my time and get out of this dump.
st1sv01	You must go to the town of Rubacava, my friend, if you want to find your lost soul.
st1ma02	How do YOU know where she is?
st1sv03	I don't. But everyone who wants to get to the Ninth Underworld must cross the Sea of Lament, and therefore must go to Rubacava to get passage on a ship. As long as you get there before she does, you'll find her, but it may be quite a wait.
st1ma04	I'll wait as long as it takes.
st1sv05	Manuel? Are you...
st1sv06	...in love with her?
st1ma07	Love? Love is for the living, Sal. I'm only after her for one reason...
st1ma08	...she's my ticket out of here.
cpddo01	Mr. LeMans, I assure you the missing woman will be found. I will personally track her down myself.
cpdhe02	Just like you personally picked her up from the Land of the Living?
cpddo03	That was my intention, but Agent Calavera somehow got to her first.
cpdhe04	We gave you the fastest car, Domino. We gave you all the best clients. You had all the advantages, so how was this Calavera able to sneak in there and eat your lunch?
cpdco05	Oh, now Hector, you can't get too mad at Domino. That wasn't his fault--
cpdhe06	Oh, I can, Don. You should know I CAN get too mad. But not at Domino. After all, he wasn't in charge of this operation.
cpdhe07	At least, not until now.
cpdco08	Hector! No!
cpdco09	Agggggggk!
cpdhe10	Marigolds... Hm. Funny...
cpdhe11	For some reason, I was expecting tulips. Well, maybe Mr. Calavera, eh, Domino? Why don't you personally go down to the basement and escort him up here? The sooner he's sprouted and we can get back to business, the better.
cpdgl12	OH HEART!  HEART IS GOOD!  BE GOOD TO HEART!  DON'T TEAR OUT HEART!  HEART IS GOOD!  STRONG BEATING GOOD HEART--Hey, is that my car?
dbvma01	(Panting) Hey, enough already!
dbvgl02	Oh? Walk through someone's campfire? Ha ha!
dbvma03	I don't want to talk about it.
gtsgl01	Manny, until now we scraped along the ground like rats, but from now on, we soar! Like eagles! Yeah! LIKE EAGLES...ON...POGO STICKS!!!
gtsma02	What a relief. I was getting concerned that our transportation wasn't ostentatious enough.
gtsgl03	Get in! Or are you afraid of heights?
gtsma04	No, just motion sickness.
hlrgl01	Hello?
hlrgl02	Ms. Colomar!
hlrgl03	We're here to save you!
hlrma04	Hey, lay off the racket! The whole town's asleep!
hlrgl05	But I wanna drag race! When they get a load o' my car, we're gonna be the talk of the town! Heh.
hlrma06	You're right. We're gonna have to find a good place to hide that road show.
hlrma07	Speaking of hiding, I wonder if Meche's here already? I'm gonna go see what I can stir up. Not a bad piece of real estate, actually. It's got potential...
plgma01	Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!
plgvl02	Ohhh, tourists!
plgvl03	You gotta watch your step around here, stranger.  Rubacava ain't the quaint little port town she used to be.
plgvl04	Wwwweeell-hell-hell.  Looks like there's a new vessel in town.  Pardon me whilst I go check her out!
yr2lu01	Hey, Boss! You gonna come downstairs? I got a customer asking for ya.
yr2ma02	You know I don't like to mingle with the customers.
yr2lu03	Well, you may wanna mingle with this one.
shgma01	Meche?
shgme02	Manny. Help me. I've been lost for so long, why didn't you look for me?
shgma03	I did! You ran off!
shgma04	Why?
shgme05	Because you said I was no good. I've been all alone in the world for a whole year...
shgme06	AND IT'S ALL BECAUSE OF YOU!
shgvl07	This going to be an annual thing with you, Manny?  Every Day of the Dead, you toss your bones into the drink, and I fish 'em out? Hmph.
shgma08	I don't plan to be around that long, Velasco.  As soon as I find out where that ocean liner's going I'm after it.
shgvl09	Ha!  That ship's going to Puerto Zapato!  That's the other side of the world!  There ain't no ships going out that way but the ol' Limbo here...
shgvl10	...but--
shgma11	But nothing.  If the Limbo's my only hope, then I'm already on board.
shgvl12	Weeeeeeell, good luck, son.  That's all I got to say. Ho ho! Ha ha ha ha!
snama01	Lola?  What are you doing here?  This crowd doesn't go much for souvenir pictures.  Except, maybe of Lenin...
snalo02	Shhh!  Manny, I'm on a stakeout!  I'm gonna prove to Maximino once and for all that Olivia's no good for him.
snama03	Still hung up on Max, eh?  Take my advice, Angel.  Forget about him.  He's a gambling racketeer--
snalo04	Ha ha. Like you?
snama05	Oh, that hurts, baby.
snalo06	Shhh!  Here they come!
snavi07	Come on, sugar.  A kiss for the road.
snaol08	Oh, ick.  Don't let me down, Nick.  You're a lawyer.  You're not supposed to have feelings.
snavi09	I don't but I know a good tort when I see one.
snavi10	Hey!
snavi11	If Maximino sees that, we're gonna end up in matching terracotta pots!
snaol12	Don't be silly.
snaol13	He wouldn't hurt me.
snaol14	He LOVES me.
psots01	[Hey!  Hold still!]  Hold still!
psots02	What are you?  DEAD!  Ach!
psots04	What kind of sailor are you--OOF!--Can't handle booze, huh? 
psots05	Velasco?  Toto!  I got your boy Naranja here.
psots06	M.I.A, he is?  Well, he sober up, I send him to Limbo.  Yeah, yeah-he'll make it there by morning.  Promise!
idcvl01	Ah, what?
idcmb02d	Naranja.
idcvl03	What?  How? ... Sprouted?  But - Ah this town's going to Hell!  Sailor can't even take a two-day shore leave without watching his back... Yeah, yeah.  I'll come down in the morning.
idcvl04	(sighs)
nrema01	I think these are the words you're looking for.
nretm01	...who will stop the fat cats of industry from building these ships with the pollen of the exploited working class?
nresb02c	Yeah! ... sick 'n' tired ... Yeah! ... no more ... Yeah! Yeah!
nretm03	I say we fight back!
nresb04a	Yeah! ... sick 'n' tired ... Yeah! ... no more ... Yeah! Yeah!
nrebg05	Hmmmm. What's this? Maybe a bee agitator?
nretm06	I say lay down your tools right now and show the man just who makes the honey around here!
nrebg07	That does it!
nresb08a	(crowd chants "Union" over and over)
nrebg09	You know, I always thought bees came in two colors: yellow and black. But you look all red to me, my friend.
nretm10	Ah! Hey! What are you doing? We've got the right to assemble peacefully!
nrebg11	Good. You're going to need a lot of assembly after we take you apart, comrade.
nretm12	Manny! Get me a lawyer! Get me a lawyer!
nresb13a	(grumble)
nrema14	Bogen? That's gonna make it tough to spring the kid and get him back out here...
lldlo01	Manny...
lldma02	Lola?
lldlo03	Careful, Manny. You may not wanna see me like this...
