svshe11a	Hee-ah, huh, uh, huh...This is where you writhe around in excruciating pain for about an hour because that idiot Bowlsley ran off with all the fast-acting Sproutella.
svshe11b	This slow stuff WILL sprout you, but it's going to take a long time, I'm sorry to say.
lsasv09a	I have reason to believe that the Bureau of Acquisitions is cheating the very souls it was chartered to serve.
lsasv09b	I think someone is robbing these poor, na╟ve souls of their rightful destinies, leaving them no option but to march on a treacherous trail of tears, unprotected and alone.
lsasv09c	Like babies, Manuel. Like babies.
lsasv13a	Well, you won't even be able to get out of this city without my help. Which means, of course, you won't be able to find that woman, and you'll never get your job back.
lsasv13b	When you're ready to join the cause, Manuel, come talk to me. We might be of some use to each other.
odjhe01a	Am I talking about just a job here? Or am I talking about opportunity, in the general sense?
odjhe01b	YOU!  Are you the one who cracked the Flores couple just now?
odjhe01c	We've had a lot of openings in this office in the last couple of years, and frankly we've had trouble filling them. I could really use a closer like you on the team.
rm3co14b	This is her reward, after a lifetime of hardship and public service? Her destiny stolen by some overreaching salesman looking for a fat commission he didn't deserve!
vmasv10a	Manuel Calavera. We meet again. I see you have found what you were looking for. How fortunate for you to arrive now just as we, too, are about to achieve success.
vmasv10b	Our army has grown, and right now our top agents are in Hector's weapons lab, about to close in on the enemy in his own den. I couldn't have done it without you, Manuel.
